(   - Equating OA from both equations:) Tj
T*
(   Ab_iso * cos\(30?\) = AB_true * cos\(45?\).) Tj
T*
(   \(Ab_iso\) / \(AB_true\) = cos\(45?\) / cos\(30?\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting trigonometric exact values \(cos 45? = 1 / sqrt\(2\); cos 30? = sqrt\(3\) / 2\):) Tj
T*
(   Isometric Length / True Length = \(1 / sqrt\(2\)\) / \(sqrt\(3\) / 2\) = 2 / \(sqrt\(2\) * sqrt\(3\)\) =) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(2\) / sqrt\(3\) = sqrt\(2 / 3\).) Tj
T*
(   Ratio = sqrt\(2/3\) = 0.8164965... ? 0.8165 \(approx 81.65% or 9/11\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Graphical Construction of an Isometric Scale:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw a horizontal reference line baseline OX.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: From point O, draw ray OA inclined at 30 degrees to OX \(representing the Isometric) Tj
T*
(   Scale line\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: From point O, draw ray OB inclined at 45 degrees to OX \(representing the True Scale) Tj
T*
(   line\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Along the 45? ray OB, mark standard true scale divisions \(0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 cm...\)) Tj
T*
(   using a standard metric ruler.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: From each marked true division point on ray OB, draw VERTICAL PROJECTOR lines) Tj
T*
(   perpendicular to baseline OX.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: The points where these vertical projectors intersect the 30? ray OA mark the) Tj
T*
(   corresponding isometric divisions \(0', 1', 2', 3'...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 7: This graduated 30? line OA is the ready-to-use Isometric Scale! Any measurement) Tj
T*
(   picked from this line represents the exact foreshortened dimension \(81.65%\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
