(   [Problem Statement]: A cylinder of base diameter 50 mm and height 70 mm rests centrally on top of a square prism of base 80 mm x 80 mm and height 30 mm. Provide complete step-by-step drafting instructions to construct its Isometric View.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step-by-Step Construction Procedure \(True Scale 1:1\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Construct the Base Square Prism \(80 x 80 x 30 mm\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw the three isometric axes from origin O \(one vertical, two at 30? to horizontal\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Along the 30? right axis, measure 80 mm \(point A\). Along the 30? left axis \(150?\),) Tj
T*
(   measure 80 mm \(point B\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Complete the bottom isometric rhombus O-A-C-B by drawing parallel lines of length 80) Tj
T*
(   mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: From vertices O, A, B, and C, erect vertical lines of height 30 mm to points O', A',) Tj
T*
(   B', C'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Join O'-A'-C'-B' to form the top isometric face of the prism.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Darken visible outer vertical edges \(A-A', O-O', B-B'\) and top boundary lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Locate Cylinder Axis & Center:) Tj
T*
(   - On the top face of the prism \(O'-A'-C'-B'\), draw diagonals A'-B' and O'-C'.) Tj
T*
(   - The intersection of the diagonals pinpoints the exact center point P of the top face.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Construct the Cylinder Base \(Lower Isocircle on Prism Face\):) Tj
T*
(   - About center P, construct an isometric rhombus of side equal to cylinder diameter 50 mm) Tj
T*
(   \(edges parallel to prism edges, spaced 25 mm on either side of center\).) Tj
T*
(   - Using the Four-Center Method, draw the lower isocircle of diameter 50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Note: Only the front half of this isocircle will be visible; the rear half is hidden under) Tj
T*
(   the cylinder body.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Construct the Cylinder Top Face \(Upper Isocircle at Height 70 mm\):) Tj
T*
(   - From center P, erect a vertical centerline of height 70 mm to establish the top center point) Tj
T*
(   Q.) Tj
T*
(   - About center Q, construct a horizontal isometric rhombus of side 50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Using the Four-Center Method, draw the complete upper isocircle \(it is 100% visible\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Draw Tangent Cylinder Outlines:) Tj
T*
(   - Draw two vertical straight lines tangent to the outermost left and right curves of the top) Tj
T*
(   and bottom isocircles.) Tj
T*
(   - Darken the visible outlines and erase internal construction lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
