(   - Function: Creates a 3D solid primitive or 3D surface by projecting a 2D planar profile) Tj
T*
(   perpendicularly \(or along an arbitrary vector\) through a specified distance.) Tj
T*
(   - Mandatory Prerequisite:) Tj
T*
(   * To generate a solid \(rather than a hollow surface\), the source profile MUST be a closed,) Tj
T*
(   planar, non-self-intersecting entity \(e.g., closed Polyline, Circle, Ellipse, or Region\).) Tj
T*
(   * Open curves or lines will generate open 3D surfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Prompt Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: EXTRUDE [Enter] -> Select objects -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: 'Specify height of extrusion or [Direction/Path/Taper angle/Expression]:') Tj
T*
(   * Direct Distance Entry: Typing a numerical value \(e.g. '50' [Enter]\) extrudes the profile) Tj
T*
(   perpendicularly along the positive Z-axis of the active UCS. Negative values extrude along) Tj
T*
(   negative Z.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Sub-Options:) Tj
T*
(   - Taper Angle \(T\):) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts for an inclination angle \(-90? to +90?\).) Tj
T*
(   * Positive taper narrows the profile inward as it ascends, creating frustums of pyramids or) Tj
T*
(   cones.) Tj
T*
(   * Negative taper flares the profile outward.) Tj
T*
(   - Path \(P\):) Tj
T*
(   * Allows extruding the 2D profile along a customized 3D trajectory curve \(Line, Polyline, Arc,) Tj
T*
(   Spline, or Helix\).) Tj
T*
(   * The profile automatically reorients normal to the path curve at every point \(ideal for curved) Tj
T*
(   piping and handrails\).) Tj
T*
(   - Direction \(D\):) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts for two points in space defining a custom directional extrusion vector.) Tj
T*
() Tj
