(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the REVOLVE command in AutoCAD, explaining axis of revolution definition, revolution angles, and rules preventing self-intersecting geometries.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. REVOLVE Command Architecture \(REV\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Sweeps a closed 2D planar profile through a circular trajectory around an axis of) Tj
T*
(   revolution to generate rotationally symmetrical 3D solids \(such as shafts, pulleys, bushings,) Tj
T*
(   spheres, and toroidal rings\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Execution Steps:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: REVOLVE [Enter] -> Select closed 2D profile -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - 'Specify axis start point or define axis by [Object/X/Y/Z] <Object>:':) Tj
T*
(   * Method A \(Two-Point Axis\): Snap to two points defining the axis of rotation using OSNAP) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., the centerline of a shaft\).) Tj
T*
(   * Method B \(Object\): Select an existing line or polyline segment as the axis.) Tj
T*
(   * Method C \(X / Y / Z\): Uses the principal axes of the active UCS passing through origin.) Tj
T*
(   - 'Specify angle of revolution or [STart angle/Reverse/Expression] <360>:':) Tj
T*
(   * Pressing Enter defaults to 360 degrees \(complete full solid of revolution\).) Tj
T*
(   * Entering a smaller angle \(e.g. 180? or 90?\) creates a partial or sectional solid.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Critical Geometric Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - The profile and the axis of revolution MUST be coplanar.) Tj
T*
(   - The axis of revolution MUST NOT intersect or cross through the interior of the profile. If) Tj
T*
(   the axis cuts through the profile, AutoCAD aborts with the fatal error: 'Cannot revolve object.) Tj
T*
(   Profile crosses axis of revolution.') Tj
T*
ET

