(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the PRESSPULL command in AutoCAD, contrasting its dynamic boundary detection with the EXTRUDE command and detailing its behavior on 3D solid faces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Dynamic PRESSPULL:) Tj
T*
(   - PRESSPULL is the most powerful and intuitive direct-modeling command in modern AutoCAD.) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike EXTRUDE \(which requires pre-formed closed polylines or regions\), PRESSPULL dynamically) Tj
T*
(   detects closed planar regions formed by any intersecting coplanar curves simply by hovering the) Tj
T*
(   cursor inside the boundary!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Operation on 2D Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   - User types PRESSPULL \(or holds Ctrl+Shift+E\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hovering inside an area bounded by overlapping lines highlights the boundary with blue dashed) Tj
T*
(   lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Clicking and moving the cursor upward instantly pulls the 2D area into a 3D solid block.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Operation on Existing 3D Solid Faces:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Face Extrusion \(Boss Creation\):) Tj
T*
(   * Clicking a planar face of an existing solid and pulling outward extends that face, increasing) Tj
T*
(   the physical dimension of the solid.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Hole Creation \(Boolean Subtraction\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw a 2D circle on the face of a 3D block.) Tj
T*
(   * Click inside the circle with PRESSPULL and push the cursor into the block.) Tj
T*
(   * AutoCAD AUTOMATICALLY performs a Boolean subtraction, cutting a clean cylindrical hole) Tj
T*
(   through the block!) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Boss on Face \(Boolean Addition\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw a circle on the face, click inside with PRESSPULL, and pull outward.) Tj
T*
(   * AutoCAD automatically unions the new cylindrical boss to the parent solid.) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates the manual multi-step workflow of Region -> Extrude -> Subtract/Union!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
