BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the 3P User Coordinate System \(UCS\) rotation method in AutoCAD, detailing how to align the drafting plane with any arbitrary inclined face of a 3D solid.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Necessity of Relocating the UCS in 3D Modeling:) Tj
T*
(   - In AutoCAD, all 2D drawing entities \(circles, rectangles, text\) are created on the active XY) Tj
T*
(   plane of the current coordinate system.) Tj
T*
(   - When modeling 3D components, features \(such as holes, slots, and bosses\) must frequently be) Tj
T*
(   placed on inclined, vertical, or compound angled faces.) Tj
T*
(   - To draft directly on an inclined surface, the UCS XY plane must be reoriented to become) Tj
T*
(   coplanar with that specific surface.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The UCS 3-Point \(3P\) Command Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: UCS [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: 'Specify origin of UCS or [Face/NAmed/OBject/Previous/View/World/X/Y/Z/ZAxis]) Tj
T*
(   <World>:' -> Type '3P' \(or '3'\) [Enter].) Tj
