(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the standard 3D Solid Primitives in AutoCAD: BOX, CYLINDER, CONE, SPHERE, TORUS, WEDGE, and PYRAMID, with their specific input parameters.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Solid Primitives Catalog:) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD provides seven built-in parametric 3D solid primitives that serve as foundational) Tj
T*
(   building blocks for complex mechanical assemblies:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Parameters and Execution:) Tj
T*
(   - BOX:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: First corner point -> Opposite corner point \(or Cube / Length option\) -> Height.) Tj
T*
(   - CYLINDER:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: Center point of base -> Base radius \(or diameter\) -> Height \(or axis endpoint for) Tj
T*
(   inclined cylinders\).) Tj
T*
(   - CONE:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: Center point of base -> Base radius -> Height \(or Top radius option to create a) Tj
T*
(   truncated frustum\).) Tj
T*
(   - SPHERE:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: Center point -> Radius \(or diameter\). Generates an exact 3D mathematical sphere.) Tj
T*
(   - TORUS \(Doughnut Solid\):) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: Center of torus -> Radius of torus \(distance from center of hole to center of tube\)) Tj
T*
(   -> Tube radius.) Tj
T*
(   * Used for O-rings, pipe bends, and handles.) Tj
T*
(   - WEDGE:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: First corner -> Opposite corner -> Height.) Tj
T*
(   * Constructs a five-sided right-angled triangular prism with an inclined top face.) Tj
T*
(   - PYRAMID:) Tj
T*
(   * Prompts: Center of base -> Base radius \(or Edge option, or Sides option from 3 to 32 sides\)) Tj
T*
(   -> Height \(or Top radius option for frustum\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. CSG \(Constructive Solid Geometry\) Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - Complex mechanical parts are created rapidly by combining these basic primitives using) Tj
T*
(   Boolean UNION, SUBTRACT, and INTERSECT.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
