(   Step-by-Step Isometric View Construction \(True Scale 1:1\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Establish Isometric Axes and Enclosing Box:) Tj
T*
(   - Length \(X\) = 100 mm, Width \(Y\) = 60 mm, Height \(Z\) = 80 mm total \(20 base + 60 upright\).) Tj
T*
(   - From origin O, draw isometric axes: X along 30? to right, Y along 150? to left, Z vertically) Tj
T*
(   at 90?.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Construct Base Plate \(100 x 60 x 20 mm\):) Tj
T*
(   - Measure 100 mm along 30? axis \(point A\). Measure 60 mm along 150? axis \(point B\).) Tj
T*
(   - Draw bottom rhombus O-A-C-B.) Tj
T*
(   - From O, A, C, B, erect vertical lines of height 20 mm to points O1, A1, C1, B1.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw top face of base plate O1-A1-C1-B1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Construct Vertical Upright \(20 mm thick x 60 mm high at left end\):) Tj
T*
(   - The upright sits at the left end of the base \(from X = 0 to X = 20, Y = 0 to 60\).) Tj
T*
(   - From O1 and B1, erect vertical lines of height 60 mm to points O2 and B2 \(Total Z = 80 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - From points at X = 20 on the top of the base, erect vertical lines of height 60 mm to points) Tj
T*
(   E and F.) Tj
T*
(   - Connect O2-B2-F-E to form the top horizontal face of the upright \(20 mm x 60 mm\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Construct the Horizontal Hole \(Diameter 30 mm through the 20 mm Upright\):) Tj
T*
(   - The hole axis is parallel to the X-axis \(drilled horizontally from X = 0 to 20\).) Tj
T*
(   - Center location: Y = 30 mm \(midpoint of upright width\), Z = 20 + 30 = 50 mm \(centered on) Tj
T*
(   upright height\).) Tj
T*
(   - Locate center point P on the front face \(X = 20\) and point Q on the back face \(X = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - The hole lies on Isoplane Left \(vertical plane defined by 90? and 150? axes\).) Tj
T*
(   - On the front face \(at X = 20\), construct an isometric rhombus of side 30 mm centered at P.) Tj
T*
(   - Using the Four-Center Method, draw the complete visible isometric ellipse of diameter 30 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - At the rear face \(X = 0\), draw the visible portion of the rear ellipse \(front-lower curve\)) Tj
T*
(   seen through the 20 mm bore.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Line Weight Finishing:) Tj
T*
(   - Darken all outer visible outlines with continuous thick lines \(Type A\).) Tj
T*
(   - Erase construction diagonals and internal hidden edges.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
