(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the rules and techniques for Isometric Dimensioning according to ISO and BIS standards, detailing aligned text, extension line directions, and leader callouts for isocircles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Isometric Dimensioning Principles:) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike 2D orthographic dimensioning \(where dimensions are purely horizontal or vertical\),) Tj
T*
(   isometric dimensions must appear to lie physically within the three-dimensional isometric) Tj
T*
(   planes of the drawing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Orientation of Dimension and Extension Lines:) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension Lines: Must be drawn strictly PARALLEL to the isometric axis along which the) Tj
T*
(   dimension is measured \(e.g., parallel to 30? axis for lengths, parallel to 150? axis for) Tj
T*
(   widths, vertical 90? for heights\).) Tj
T*
(   - Extension Lines: Must project outward from the feature PARALLEL to an adjacent isometric axis) Tj
T*
(   \(never perpendicular to the dimension line!\).) Tj
T*
(   - Arrowheads: Must be drawn slender and elongated \(ratio 3:1\), aligned parallel to the) Tj
T*
(   dimension line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Text Alignment \(Aligned vs Oblique Text\):) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
