(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of creating 3D solids by SWEEP and LOFT in AutoCAD, comparing their geometric inputs, guide curves, and practical engineering applications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. SWEEP Command:) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Sweeps a closed 2D planar profile along a customized 1D trajectory path curve) Tj
T*
(   \(which can be a 2D or 3D curve\) to generate complex extruded tubular solids, coiled springs,) Tj
T*
(   and ducting.) Tj
T*
(   - Parameters & Inputs:) Tj
T*
(   * Profile: Closed polyline, circle, ellipse, or region.) Tj
T*
(   * Sweep Path: Spline, 3D polyline, helix, or arc.) Tj
T*
(   * Alignment: Profile automatically aligns perpendicular to the start tangent of the path.) Tj
T*
(   * Scale & Twist: Can taper the profile along the path or twist it through specified angular) Tj
T*
(   turns \(e.g. creating drill bit flutes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Application: HVAC exhaust ducting, bent hydraulic pipelines, coiled springs, and wiring) Tj
T*
(   harnesses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. LOFT Command:) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates a smooth, continuous 3D solid that transitions seamlessly between TWO OR) Tj
T*
(   MORE distinct cross-sectional profiles \(called 'cross sections' or 'ribs'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Parameters & Inputs:) Tj
T*
(   * Profiles: Series of 2D closed curves arranged in space \(e.g., transitioning from a square) Tj
T*
(   base to an elliptical mid-section to a circular top\).) Tj
T*
(   * Guides: Longitudinal curves that define the outer surface contours between profiles.) Tj
T*
(   * Path Curve: A single central spine governing the loft trajectory.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Aerodynamic aircraft wings, boat hulls, exhaust turbine manifolds, and ergonomic) Tj
T*
(   mouse enclosures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   - SWEEP maintains a single constant profile \(or uniform scale/twist\) along a path.) Tj
T*
(   - LOFT morphs between completely different geometric shapes across multiple stages.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
