(   [Problem Statement]: A square prism \(base 50 mm, height 70 mm\) has a cylindrical hole of 30 mm diameter drilled centrally from top to bottom. Provide the AutoCAD command sequence to draw its 2D isometric view using ISODRAFT mode.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD 2D Isometric Drafting Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   1. Setup Isometric Mode:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: ISODRAFT [Enter] -> Option: isoplaneTop \(or press F5 until Isoplane Top is active\).) Tj
T*
(   - Turn ON Ortho \(F8\). Ensure OSNAP is ON \(F3: Endpoint, Midpoint, Intersection\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Draw Top Isometric Face of Prism \(at Z = 70 mm\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE [Enter] -> Start point: 100,150 [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Next point: @50<30 [Enter] -> Next: @50<150 [Enter] -> Next: @50<-150 [Enter] -> Close: C) Tj
T*
(   [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Result: Top rhombus of the 50 mm square prism.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Draw Vertical Prism Outlines:) Tj
T*
(   - Switch to Isoplane Right or Left \(F5\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> From right corner: @70<-90 [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> From bottom-center corner: @70<-90 [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LINE -> From left corner: @70<-90 [Enter].) Tj
T*
