/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Sectional Isometric View, detailing how a 90-degree quadrant is removed from a 3D isometric model and how hatching angles are determined on isometric cut faces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose and Concept of Sectional Isometric Views:) Tj
T*
(   - When an isometric pictorial drawing is created for an assembly containing intricate internal) Tj
T*
(   components \(valves, gear pumps, engine cylinders\), external views hide the internal mechanisms.) Tj
T*
(   - A Sectional Isometric View reveals both external features and internal assemblies) Tj
T*
(   simultaneously by mentally cutting away a 90-degree quadrant \(one-quarter of the object\) from) Tj
T*
(   the front.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Cutting Plane Orientation:) Tj
T*
(   - Two perpendicular cutting planes are passed through the central symmetry axes of the object:) Tj
T*
(   * One plane lies along the 30? isometric axis \(Isoplane Right\).) Tj
T*
(   * The second plane lies along the 150? isometric axis \(Isoplane Left\).) Tj
T*
(   - The front quadrant between these planes is removed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Section Lining \(Hatching\) Rules on Isometric Cut Faces:) Tj
T*
(   - Standard 45? hatching cannot be applied blindly because 45? is not an isometric angle.) Tj
T*
(   - Isometric Hatching Rule \(ISO / BIS SP 46\):) Tj
T*
(   * Hatching lines on isometric cut faces are drawn PARALLEL TO THE ISOMETRIC AXES or conjugate) Tj
T*
(   diagonals of the cut face!) Tj
T*
(   * Cut face on Isoplane Left: Hatching lines are drawn at 60 degrees to the horizontal \(sloping) Tj
T*
(   upwards to the left\).) Tj
T*
(   * Cut face on Isoplane Right: Hatching lines are drawn at 60 degrees to the horizontal \(sloping) Tj
T*
(   upwards to the right\).) Tj
T*
(   * Adjacent mating components in an assembly are hatched in opposing directions \(e.g. 60? left) Tj
T*
(   vs 60? right\) or with varying line spacing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
