(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of creating 3D Solids in AutoCAD using the POLYSOLID command, detailing wall height, width, and arc-segment options.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of POLYSOLID:) Tj
T*
(   - POLYSOLID is an AutoCAD 3D solid modeling command that creates continuous rectangular-walled) Tj
T*
(   3D solid structures analogous to a 2D polyline, but with integrated physical wall thickness) Tj
T*
(   \(width\) and vertical height.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Widely utilized in civil, architectural, and structural modeling for rapid) Tj
T*
(   layout of building walls, retaining barriers, and machine enclosure housings.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Parameters and Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: POLYSOLID \(or 'PSOLID' [Enter]\)) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: 'Specify start point or [Object/Height/Width/Justification] <Object>:') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Configuration Sub-Options:) Tj
T*
(   - Height \(H\): Sets the vertical extrusion height of the wall \(e.g. 2400 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Width \(W\): Sets the horizontal wall thickness \(e.g. 200 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Justification \(J\): Sets whether the wall is aligned:) Tj
T*
(   * Center: Wall is centered on the picked path line.) Tj
T*
(   * Left: Wall projects to the left of the path.) Tj
T*
(   * Right: Wall projects to the right of the path.) Tj
T*
ET

