(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the INTERSECT and INTERFERE commands in AutoCAD, explaining Boolean intersection modeling and 3D interference checking in mechanical assemblies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. INTERSECT Command \(IN\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Performs a Boolean intersection between two or more overlapping 3D solids \(or 2D) Tj
T*
(   regions\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Operation: Retains ONLY the volume shared in common by ALL selected solids,) Tj
T*
(   completely discarding all non-overlapping volumes.) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Scenario: Modeling complex curved turbine blades or compound aerospace fittings) Tj
T*
(   by intersecting two orthogonal extrusions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. INTERFERE Command \(INF\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Performs automated collision and clash detection between 3D solids in mechanical) Tj
T*
(   assemblies without altering or destroying the original components!) Tj
T*
(   - Command Execution Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   * Command: INTERFERE [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   * Select first set of solids \(e.g. rotating drive shaft assembly\) -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   * Select second set of solids \(e.g. stationary machine frame\) -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Diagnostic Output:) Tj
T*
(   * AutoCAD analyzes all 3D solid boundary surfaces for physical overlap.) Tj
T*
(   * If clashes exist, AutoCAD highlights the overlapping volumes in bright red and creates a) Tj
T*
(   temporary 3D solid representing the exact interference volume!) Tj
T*
(   * Displays a dialog box reporting: 'Interfering pairs: 2. Volume: 142.50 cu mm.') Tj
T*
(   - Value: Critical quality assurance step to eliminate mechanical jamming before sending CAD) Tj
T*
(   files to CNC machining.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
