(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the procedure to generate 2D Orthographic Views from a 3D Solid Model in AutoCAD using the VIEWBASE and FLATSHOT commands.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. VIEWBASE Command \(Modern Standard\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Automatically generates associative 2D orthographic front, top, side, and isometric) Tj
T*
(   views from a 3D model directly in Paper Space layouts.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   * Switch to a Layout tab \(Paper Space\).) Tj
T*
(   * Command: VIEWBASE [Enter] -> Option: 'From Model Space'.) Tj
T*
(   * Select 3D solids -> Press Enter.) Tj
T*
(   * Place Base View \(e.g. Front View\) on the sheet -> Click.) Tj
T*
(   * Move cursor upward: AutoCAD automatically projects the Top View.) Tj
T*
(   * Move cursor to the right: Projects the Right Side View.) Tj
T*
(   * Move cursor diagonally: Projects a shaded 3D Isometric View!) Tj
T*
(   * Press Enter to finalize.) Tj
T*
(   - Associativity: If the 3D solid model in model space is modified, all 2D views on the layout) Tj
T*
(   update automatically!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. FLATSHOT Command \(In-Model Vector Flattening\):) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Creates a flat 2D block representing the current 3D viewport projection placed) Tj
T*
