T*
(   - Behavior: Offsets every face vertex along its surface normal vector and sews the perimeter) Tj
T*
(   edges with solid walls.) Tj
T*
(   - Application: Creating stamped sheet metal brackets, aerodynamic fairings, and composite shell) Tj
T*
(   components from imported CAD surfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. CONVTOSOLID Command:) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Converts eligible 3D objects \(such as closed 2D polylines with thickness, 3D meshes) Tj
T*
(   with watertight volumes, and closed planar 3D faces\) into standard 3D solid primitives.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   * Command: CONVTOSOLID [Enter] -> Select eligible entities -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Topological Limitations:) Tj
T*
(   * The input object MUST form a completely watertight volume \(manifold geometry\) without) Tj
T*
(   self-intersecting faces, T-junctions, or missing boundary patches.) Tj
T*
(   * If the mesh has even a microscopic hole, AutoCAD aborts with 'Object cannot be converted to a) Tj
T*
(   solid.') Tj
T*
